// A purchase agreement for 14 Alder Lane between Nora Whitfield and Omar Reyes (purchase.md).
Document "purchase.md"

Fact seller Identified by Nora
Fact buyer Identified by Omar
Fact escrow-agent Identified by HarborTitle
Fact usd Identified by Money(USD, 2)
Param price : Money(USD, 2) = 40000000
Param earnest : Money(USD, 2) = 1000000

// 1. Sale: binding once both have signed; open until closed or cancelled
Bool seller-signed
Bool buyer-signed
Act seller-signs Actor seller Holds when True Creates seller-signed()
Act buyer-signs Actor buyer Holds when True Creates buyer-signed()
Bool signed Holds when seller-signed() && buyer-signed()
Bool cancelled
Bool open Holds when signed() && Not(cancelled()) && Not(closed())

// 2. Earnest money: due in three days, held in escrow, paid out only as the agreement says
Bool in-escrow
Bool refundable
Bool forfeited
Duty earnest-due Holder buyer Claimant seller
  Holds when open() && Not(in-escrow())
  Due within 3
Act pay-earnest Actor buyer Recipient escrow-agent Related to usd
  Holds when open()
  Valid when usd == earnest
  Creates in-escrow()
Act refund Actor escrow-agent Recipient buyer
  Holds when in-escrow() && refundable()
  Terminates in-escrow()
Act pay-seller Actor escrow-agent Recipient seller
  Holds when in-escrow() && (closed() || forfeited())
  Terminates in-escrow()
Power cancel-for-no-earnest Actor seller Recipient buyer
  Holds when True
  Valid when Violated(earnest-due())
  Creates cancelled()

// 3. Inspection: ten days
Power cancel-on-inspection Actor buyer Recipient seller
  Holds when True
  Valid when open() && Not(Held(signed()) For 10)
  Creates cancelled(), refundable()

// 4. Financing: thirty days
Bool loan-committed
Event lender-commits Creates loan-committed()
Power cancel-on-financing Actor buyer Recipient seller
  Holds when True
  Valid when open() && Not(loan-committed()) && Not(Held(signed()) For 30)
  Creates cancelled(), refundable()

// 5. Closing: the rest of the price and the deed, within forty-five days
Var paid Identified by Money(USD, 2)
Bool deed-delivered
Duty balance-due Holder buyer Claimant seller
  Holds when open() && paid < price - earnest
  Due within 45
Act pay-price Actor buyer Recipient seller Related to usd
  Holds when open()
  Creates paid(paid + usd)
Duty deed-due Holder seller Claimant buyer
  Holds when open() && Not(deed-delivered())
  Due within 45
Act deliver-deed Actor seller Recipient buyer
  Holds when open()
  Creates deed-delivered()
Bool closed Holds when deed-delivered() && paid >= price - earnest

// 6. Default
Power cancel-for-no-deed Actor buyer Recipient seller
  Holds when True
  Valid when Violated(deed-due())
  Creates cancelled(), refundable()
Power cancel-for-no-payment Actor seller Recipient buyer
  Holds when True
  Valid when Violated(balance-due())
  Creates cancelled(), forfeited()

// 7. Risk of loss
Bool destroyed
Event house-destroyed Creates destroyed()
Power cancel-on-loss Actor buyer Recipient seller
  Holds when True
  Valid when open() && destroyed()
  Creates cancelled(), refundable()

Clause 1.1 Approved "03735c1e471b23c65ecb1eabc37020fe68035388af1cc7f44ae824d194751722"
  Norm "Nora Whitfield, the seller, sells the house at 14 Alder Lane to Omar Reyes, the buyer, for four hundred thousand dollars." => pay-price, deliver-deed
Clause 1.2 Approved "9a0e8644163d8dbbf61182ef9af4efc7ea9386adf089c95253fd534d4048be46"
  Norm "This agreement binds the parties once both of them have signed it." => seller-signs, buyer-signs
  Definition " The day the second of them signs is the signing day."
Clause 2.1 Approved "83524afaa747d26994bc1023622e8b8837d65cda34b40799c1c01e501606a978"
  Norm "Within three days after the signing day the buyer pays earnest money of ten thousand dollars to Harbor Title, the escrow agent." => earnest-due, pay-earnest
Clause 2.2 Approved "e2a5b5fd21c107e1de19df8245e347fc2693545ec076eae321f62e885d622e14"
  Norm "The escrow agent holds the earnest money and pays it out only as this agreement says." => refund, pay-seller
Clause 2.3 Approved "288f37cf205954a56ad8839c9389540d351c53b575d911019e9de8a6654da755"
  Norm "If the earnest money is not paid in time, the seller may cancel this agreement." => cancel-for-no-earnest
Clause 3.1 Approved "c5d7066813ace4d511d469f589277ae357a447ad2fd3696b7f1a7a68c6f17462"
  Norm "For ten days after the signing day the buyer may have the house inspected and may cancel this agreement for any reason." => cancel-on-inspection
  Norm " If the buyer cancels under this section, the earnest money is returned to the buyer." => cancel-on-inspection, refund
Clause 4.1 Approved "2ca4df1b14f59bfc9b901897c4fc73b215366b0ae70f229e9a4d014472cdf154"
  Definition "This sale depends on the buyer obtaining a loan."
  Norm " For thirty days after the signing day the buyer may cancel this agreement if no lender has committed to make the loan." => cancel-on-financing
  Norm " If the buyer cancels under this section, the earnest money is returned to the buyer." => cancel-on-financing, refund
Clause 5.1 Approved "da0e19817d9651d7293c746b8bfbe6cbb1eb28418e852efbd4aa0fd474737048"
  Norm "Closing takes place within forty-five days after the signing day." => balance-due, deed-due
  Norm " At closing the buyer pays the seller the rest of the price and the seller delivers the deed to the buyer." => pay-price, deliver-deed
Clause 5.2 Approved "43bb1d5158aca990fc409b841c7013665ed7222849d30bda197a6bf6956d4e34"
  Norm "When both have been done the sale is closed: title to the house passes to the buyer, and the earnest money is paid to the seller as part of the price." => pay-seller
Clause 6.1 Approved "ede0f6e0c7036a77abf774e6ee8a615c49ee196f1660d98557dd6589f18cc84b"
  Norm "If the seller does not deliver the deed in time, the buyer may cancel this agreement and the earnest money is returned to the buyer." => cancel-for-no-deed, refund
Clause 6.2 Approved "9a47e41d0217e9a3574faa1a57a227e8209eefe7a7fcd55f31c9eaa5526e4b56"
  Norm "If the buyer does not pay the rest of the price in time, the seller may cancel this agreement and keeps the earnest money." => cancel-for-no-payment, pay-seller
Clause 7.1 Approved "98f936840cb12954b6e29c581e29fe37996114f5a2e10a3e78d935485e684d7d"
  Definition "Until closing the risk of loss stays with the seller."
  Norm " If the house is destroyed before closing, the buyer may cancel this agreement and the earnest money is returned to the buyer." => cancel-on-loss, refund
Clause 8.1 Approved "88a129567686665d1d7b1da6abeb840faca56ba2973d239abc2b3a0c84fec725"
  Norm "A cancellation that this agreement does not allow has no effect." => cancel-for-no-earnest, cancel-on-inspection, cancel-on-financing, cancel-for-no-deed, cancel-for-no-payment, cancel-on-loss
  Norm " Once this agreement is cancelled, neither party owes the other anything more under it." => earnest-due, balance-due, deed-due
.
+paid(0).
